# the parser of the machine form text
#
# it reads through the parser of the ir text form, so the lexer, the header and
# the refusals with their line and column are that form's. the text is read in
# two passes over a function: the first makes its virtual registers, slots and
# blocks, so an operand can name a block written after it, and the second
# appends each instruction, checked against its opcode's row. a register and an
# instruction are looked up by the rows of the set's register file and catalog,
# and a name those rows do not hold is refused.

